-- title:
--   Splitting S → A with kernel tS over a local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative local ring with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A$, let $S$ be a commutative ring equipped with an $A$-algebra structure, and let $t \in S$; write $I = tS$ for the ideal generated by $t$. Assume: (i) the quotient $S/I$ is a finite $A$-module; (ii) the structure map $A \to S/I$ is injective; and (iii) for every $s \in S$ there is $a \in A$ with $s - a\cdot 1_S$ lying in the sum $I + \mathfrak m_A S$ of the ideal $tS$ and the image ideal of $\mathfrak m_A$ under $A \to S$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\chi : S \to A$ such that $\chi(a \cdot 1_S) = a$ for all $a \in A$ (so $\chi$ splits the structure map $A \to S$), and such that the kernel of $\chi$ is exactly the ideal generated by $t$. Thus $A \to S/tS$ is an isomorphism, realised by a retraction of $S$ onto $A$ with kernel $tS$.
--
--   A statement of commutative algebra: a finite, faithful quotient $S/tS$ of an $A$-algebra which is generated by $A$ modulo the maximal ideal is the base ring itself, yielding a section of $S$ over $A$ cutting out $t$. It is used in the construction of sections of an algebraic curve through a smooth point of the special fibre, in [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_section_localRing_apply_eq_of_ord_eq_one_of_mem_smoothLocus).
